1
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:35,030
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:37,720
[Episode 8]

3
00:01:38,759 --> 00:01:39,470
Mr. Li.

4
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:41,240
Have they interrogated you?

5
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:42,680
What crimes are you

6
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:43,680
and Director Hong accused of?

7
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:45,280
They've interrogated me twice,

8
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:47,280
accusing me of covering for criminals

9
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:49,410
and leaking important state secrets.

10
00:01:49,870 --> 00:01:52,000
Don't discuss the details of the case.

11
00:01:52,870 --> 00:01:53,420
Okay.

12
00:01:54,070 --> 00:01:55,470
We... We will be careful.

13
00:01:56,729 --> 00:01:58,000
Does the crime of covering for criminals

14
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,920
refer to defending Qiao Zhiliang?

15
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:00,420
Yes.

16
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:01,640
What about leaking state secrets?

17
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:02,350
What does it refer to?

18
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:03,230
What's going on?

19
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:05,890
I told you
not to discuss the details of the case.

20
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,280
Okay, okay, okay.

21
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:07,920
Okay.

22
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:14,360
Can you speak English?

23
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,079
A little.

24
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:25,590
What kind of state secrets

25
00:02:26,190 --> 00:02:28,240
do they mean?

26
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:33,079
When I met Qiao Zhiliang,

27
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:34,750
he was determined to die.

28
00:02:34,750 --> 00:02:36,430
To dissuade him, I told him

29
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,840
the procuratorate

30
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:40,030
was preparing to
recommend the death penalty.

31
00:02:40,030 --> 00:02:40,829
They believed

32
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:42,710
that was leaking state secrets.

33
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:44,000
I'm warning you one last time.

34
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:44,710
If you discuss
the details of the case again,

35
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:47,240
the meeting
will be terminated immediately.

36
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:50,310
Well, well, well...

37
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:51,960
If we can't
discuss the details of the case,

38
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,090
what are we here for?

39
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:54,730
Which law stipulates that

40
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:57,960
lawyers cannot discuss case details
while meeting clients?

41
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,240
Improve your attitude.

42
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,340
If you correct your mistake,

43
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:01,800
I will change my attitude!

44
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,710
Calm down.

45
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:17,710
Sit down!

46
00:03:17,810 --> 00:03:19,070
I'll just be standing.

47
00:03:39,870 --> 00:03:40,510
Now,

48
00:03:41,030 --> 00:03:43,160
let's discuss the details of the case.

49
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:45,710
Is that okay, Officer?

50
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:55,120
Do you know
Chen Yizhong is also detained here?

51
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:56,470
Why?

52
00:03:57,590 --> 00:03:58,590
Just wait and see.

53
00:03:58,770 --> 00:03:59,940
Let the storm rage

54
00:03:59,970 --> 00:04:00,970
more fiercely!

55
00:04:01,910 --> 00:04:02,780
More fiercely.

56
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:07,520
Lu told me about

57
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,180
the process of their meeting.

58
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:12,560
I think Li Xiang's case is a good thing.

59
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:13,290
A good thing?

60
00:04:13,870 --> 00:04:14,520
If this case's impact

61
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:15,680
is large enough,

62
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,740
I think it will be a good

63
00:04:19,950 --> 00:04:21,480
legal education campaign.

64
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,510
It can correct people's misconceptions

65
00:04:23,510 --> 00:04:24,370
about lawyers.

66
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:26,600
I even hope that

67
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:28,490
the first trial

68
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:32,230
can find Li Xiang guilty.

69
00:04:39,430 --> 00:04:40,430
In this way, this case will become

70
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:41,480
a very classic case

71
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,720
in our country.

72
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:45,490
But it's too risky.

73
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,680
Even if they win the lawsuit,

74
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,610
their careers will be ruined, too.

75
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:51,390
What's more, to fight all the way
to the Supreme People's Court,

76
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:52,159
how long will they have to

77
00:04:52,159 --> 00:04:52,960
stay in there?

78
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:55,280
If they can't overturn the case,

79
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:57,360
their whole lives will be over.

80
00:04:57,470 --> 00:04:58,600
What about Yizhong?

81
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,120
I stand by what I said.

82
00:05:01,190 --> 00:05:02,310
The progress of the legal system

83
00:05:02,310 --> 00:05:04,370
requires some people's dedication.

84
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,750
I believe Yizhong is also prepared

85
00:05:05,750 --> 00:05:06,880
to make sacrifices.

86
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:10,360
You keep talking about

87
00:05:10,390 --> 00:05:11,560
sacrificing Li Xiang and Chen Yizhong.

88
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:12,270
How's that different from

89
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,160
them arresting Li Xiang?

90
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,620
That's not the same thing.

91
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:17,120
When they arrested Li Xiang,

92
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,830
they probably genuinely thought that

93
00:05:18,830 --> 00:05:19,770
they were keeping the people in mind

94
00:05:19,770 --> 00:05:22,030
and eliminating threats for the people.

95
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,120
If this case

96
00:05:26,270 --> 00:05:27,240
is only about

97
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,770
saving Li Xiang from there,

98
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,510
then the significance of this case

99
00:05:30,510 --> 00:05:31,640
will be too trivial.

100
00:05:32,150 --> 00:05:33,159
I believe Yizhong's original intention

101
00:05:33,159 --> 00:05:33,890
wasn't like this, either.

102
00:05:33,890 --> 00:05:35,950
He was seeking to fulfill his ideals.

103
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,390
Mr. Lu, who grew up in the city,

104
00:05:43,390 --> 00:05:44,040
probably doesn't know

105
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,240
what sacrifices are.

106
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:46,750
Cadre Yu,

107
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,570
who are you looking down on?

108
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:52,500
S-So you're the only one who has watched
Heroic Sons and Daughters?

109
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:53,610
Why don't you make sacrifices?

110
00:05:53,610 --> 00:05:55,740
I'll make sacrifices when necessary.

111
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:57,750
Most sacrifices

112
00:05:57,750 --> 00:05:58,850
are made anonymously,

113
00:05:58,850 --> 00:05:59,770
just like dust.

114
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,560
Those who only focus on money

115
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,310
wouldn't understand.

116
00:06:03,310 --> 00:06:04,380
I-I don't understand?

117
00:06:04,380 --> 00:06:06,440
That's right. You don't understand.

118
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,000
The tuition fees
for my four years of college study

119
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,400
were pooled together by the whole village.

120
00:06:18,630 --> 00:06:19,240
I left the village,

121
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:20,570
but my younger siblings

122
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:21,880
have to stay at home,

123
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:23,610
farming the land

124
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,890
and taking care of our parents.

125
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,530
They can't study at school.

126
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:30,750
You guys can only see me,

127
00:06:30,750 --> 00:06:32,880
but you can't see the people behind me.

128
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,060
To exchange my life

129
00:06:38,190 --> 00:06:39,920
for the progress of the system,

130
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,120
and leave a name in the history
of the Chinese legal system,

131
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,380
I am willing to do that.

132
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:47,830
He was talking about dust a while ago,

133
00:06:47,830 --> 00:06:50,290
and now he wants to
leave his name in history.

134
00:06:52,630 --> 00:06:55,090
My heart remains
as pure as ice in a jade vase.

135
00:06:57,510 --> 00:06:58,440
Enjoy your meal.

136
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:09,910
Why did you have to
add that last sentence?

137
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:14,120
That's the only line he knows.

138
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:16,850
He couldn't even
come up with the first half of it.

139
00:07:16,950 --> 00:07:18,310
Who knows that the food on our plates

140
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:19,510
comes from hard work?

141
00:07:20,870 --> 00:07:22,930
If you're not eating it, give it to me.

142
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:30,000
Hello.

143
00:07:30,830 --> 00:07:32,290
It's me, Ding Zhongxiang.

144
00:07:33,270 --> 00:07:35,240
Regarding the case
of Hong Zhansheng and Li Xiang,

145
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,370
your procuratorate

146
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:38,409
must make it well-grounded for me.

147
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:39,560
What?

148
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,980
This might lead to a serious problem.

149
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,510
According to the detention center,

150
00:07:46,510 --> 00:07:48,390
several groups of people have come.

151
00:07:48,390 --> 00:07:51,390
They insisted on
acting as Li Xiang's defense lawyers.

152
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,240
Well, Ding,

153
00:07:52,909 --> 00:07:53,680
these lawyers

154
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,070
are all from the city.

155
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,070
They're very arrogant.

156
00:07:59,190 --> 00:07:59,510
I...

157
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:08,560
How did the lawyers
from the provincial capital

158
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,070
find out about this?

159
00:08:10,710 --> 00:08:12,410
The provincial bar association

160
00:08:12,410 --> 00:08:13,270
must have told them to do this.

161
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:15,730
Then how did
the provincial bar association

162
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:17,000
find out about this?

163
00:08:17,310 --> 00:08:18,360
Someone must have

164
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,310
tipped them off.

165
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,000
Then who

166
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,870
tipped them off?

167
00:08:27,510 --> 00:08:27,970
Well...

168
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:30,240
Ding, how would I know?

169
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:31,680
But I think this move

170
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:32,669
is quite insidious.

171
00:08:32,669 --> 00:08:33,510
How come this mess

172
00:08:33,510 --> 00:08:35,169
is getting bigger and bigger?

173
00:08:36,669 --> 00:08:38,530
Then you'd better handle it well.

174
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:40,549
Don't let go.

175
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:41,909
Ding.

176
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,750
I won't take the blame, either.

177
00:08:48,710 --> 00:08:50,870
There's one more thing I need to tell you.

178
00:08:50,870 --> 00:08:53,270
The higher-ups ordered me

179
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,300
to prosecute Chen Yizhong

180
00:08:55,510 --> 00:08:57,670
for the crime of counter-revolution.

181
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:01,550
Yu Gaoyuan.

182
00:09:06,150 --> 00:09:07,030
Lu Zeming.

183
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:14,800
I'm going out for a bit.

184
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:22,240
Go inside.

185
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:24,010
Stop sneaking around.

186
00:09:27,270 --> 00:09:28,070
What's wrong?

187
00:09:29,390 --> 00:09:32,050
A few lawyers
came from the provincial capital.

188
00:09:32,870 --> 00:09:34,670
They want to represent Li Xiang.

189
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:37,030
Well, how did they find out about it?

190
00:09:37,030 --> 00:09:38,440
I... I think it's due to

191
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,300
the help of the newspaper office.

192
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:42,700
It's possible.

193
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:45,270
Li Xiang is a member
of the bar association.

194
00:09:45,270 --> 00:09:47,550
The newspaper office reported it
to the provincial bar association,

195
00:09:47,550 --> 00:09:49,480
and those lawyers
couldn't just sit there doing nothing.

196
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,630
They usually feel wronged,

197
00:09:50,630 --> 00:09:52,360
and now they are making an issue of it.

198
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,150
What do you mean by making an issue of it?

199
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:55,080
This is actually a real issue.

200
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,360
Anyway, now Li Xiang's case is not

201
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,960
just about Li Xiang anymore.

202
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,870
Those bureaucrats certainly didn't expect

203
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:00,600
a small place like Nanyu

204
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,930
would become famous because of this case.

205
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:04,240
Get maximum results with minimum effort.

206
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,170
Amazing, Lihui.

207
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:09,520
Wait, wait, wait.

208
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:10,870
These lawyers didn't mention

209
00:10:10,870 --> 00:10:12,530
releasing Chen Yizhong, huh?

210
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:14,840
No.

211
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:17,530
Then didn't he really become a sacrifice?

212
00:10:17,670 --> 00:10:19,130
We need to find a solution.

213
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,080
Comrades.

214
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,000
How about we add fuel to the fire?

215
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,300
Let's go to Beijing

216
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:42,960
and talk to Zhou Yipu
and Cheng Jianji directly.

217
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:43,630
They couldn't possibly

218
00:10:43,630 --> 00:10:45,000
watch their favorite student

219
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,600
get locked up like this, huh?

220
00:10:47,550 --> 00:10:48,120
Look.

221
00:10:48,150 --> 00:10:49,390
A perfectly good thing sounds negative

222
00:10:49,390 --> 00:10:50,650
when you talk about it.

223
00:10:51,310 --> 00:10:52,000
There isn't even a charge

224
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,270
against Chen Yizhong now.

225
00:10:53,270 --> 00:10:54,120
Mr. Zhou and the others

226
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:55,630
might also have no way to intervene.

227
00:10:55,630 --> 00:10:57,280
Ding Zhongxiang
is also troubled by this now.

228
00:10:57,280 --> 00:10:59,610
He doesn't dare to release or convict him.

229
00:11:00,030 --> 00:11:01,010
What did you say?

230
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:03,820
The crime of counter-revolution?

231
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:05,000
What are you guys trying to do?

232
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,550
That's why I'm discussing it with you.

233
00:11:06,550 --> 00:11:07,840
I'm telling you, Guan!

234
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,200
If you dare to do this,

235
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:11,840
both of us will have to bear

236
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:14,240
historical responsibility in the future.

237
00:11:14,270 --> 00:11:15,960
An immature student

238
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,050
complained a bit,

239
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,600
and now he's accused
of the crime of counter-revolution.

240
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:19,500
Calm down first.

241
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:20,230
Calm down.

242
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:21,390
Do you think he has

243
00:11:21,390 --> 00:11:23,120
a counter-revolutionary tendency?

244
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:24,010
I know.

245
00:11:24,910 --> 00:11:26,110
How about we find a way

246
00:11:27,030 --> 00:11:30,230
and handle it as the crime
of obstructing public affairs?

247
00:11:30,630 --> 00:11:31,600
What do you think?

248
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:34,400
After all,
he did break into the detention center.

249
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,630
Are we shopping and bargaining here?

250
00:11:38,630 --> 00:11:38,960
No.

251
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:40,230
What?

252
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:42,520
If you really dare to send the file over,

253
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:44,200
I will definitely reject it.

254
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:47,600
Even if you dare to send it,
I won't accept it, either!

255
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,800
Ding, let me tell you.

256
00:11:49,150 --> 00:11:50,440
This boy, Chen Yizhong...

257
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:52,050
Emotionally, morally and legally,

258
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:53,580
I think he's just a good kid.

259
00:11:56,870 --> 00:11:57,360
Well...

260
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,400
Let's drag it out for now.

261
00:12:01,150 --> 00:12:02,150
What do you think?

262
00:12:04,150 --> 00:12:04,630
Okay.

263
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,560
That's settled then.

264
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:09,980
I'll go to see Court Pres. Ding
to ask for leave.

265
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:10,780
Wait a minute.

266
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,030
Are you going by yourself?

267
00:12:12,030 --> 00:12:13,170
How about I... I... I...

268
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:14,080
I'll go with Yingjie.

269
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:15,200
You and Lihui can stay here.

270
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,390
Let's make a long-distance call every day

271
00:12:16,390 --> 00:12:17,320
to keep in touch.

272
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:31,560
[Court President's Office]

273
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,360
Court Pres. Ding.

274
00:12:49,790 --> 00:12:51,200
I didn't answer the phone.

275
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:52,510
What are you doing here?

276
00:12:52,510 --> 00:12:54,030
Xia Yingjie and I want to

277
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:56,620
take a few days off
and go back to Beijing.

278
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:57,910
You're going back to Beijing?

279
00:12:57,910 --> 00:12:58,320
Why?

280
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:02,030
To report the situation.

281
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:05,240
Who will you report the situation to?

282
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:06,500
Our school's mentors.

283
00:13:10,180 --> 00:13:11,910
What a waste of time and energy.

284
00:13:12,050 --> 00:13:13,240
All your behavior

285
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,640
during this one year here

286
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:18,480
will be written
into your evaluation reports.

287
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:21,210
It will follow you guys
for the rest of your lives.

288
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:23,780
Have a seat.

289
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,400
This matter with Li Xiang

290
00:13:29,750 --> 00:13:31,210
will pass sooner or later.

291
00:13:32,150 --> 00:13:33,150
In a few years,

292
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:34,240
you guys might not even

293
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,500
remember this person.

294
00:13:36,670 --> 00:13:38,000
Maybe in this lifetime,

295
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:41,050
you will never come to Nanyu again.

296
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,270
But now,

297
00:13:44,910 --> 00:13:46,510
for this person, this matter

298
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,060
and this place,

299
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,730
you are going to
sacrifice your entire lives.

300
00:13:52,670 --> 00:13:53,150
Kid,

301
00:13:54,150 --> 00:13:55,440
saying one wrong word

302
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:58,270
or picking the wrong side

303
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,120
will ruin your whole life.

304
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:05,440
There are so many lessons
to be learned from the past.

305
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:06,840
And this Qin Zhigao, too.

306
00:14:06,950 --> 00:14:07,500
Don't you think he's...

307
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,900
What about Chen Yizhong?

308
00:14:11,630 --> 00:14:12,480
What if he really

309
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,410
gets convicted?

310
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:14,930
What will you do?

311
00:14:19,390 --> 00:14:21,360
Will you rather die with honor
than live with shame,

312
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,480
or just force yourself

313
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:24,010
to swallow the bitter pill?

314
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,120
Court Pres. Ding, we're going to Beijing

315
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:28,150
for your sake, too.

316
00:14:28,150 --> 00:14:29,010
I don't need it.

317
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:39,260
What did you just say about your family?

318
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:41,390
I didn't say anything about my family.

319
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,160
The house collapsed.

320
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,860
Xia... Xia Yingjie's house collapsed, too.

321
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,500
Write a leave request.

322
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:57,380
I'll sign it when you finish.

323
00:14:59,480 --> 00:14:59,940
Listen.

324
00:15:01,870 --> 00:15:03,440
After you two leave Nanyu,

325
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:06,360
you'll no longer be under my supervision.

326
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:08,020
As for what you're going to do,

327
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:10,080
I don't care,

328
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:11,680
and I don't know.

329
00:15:12,150 --> 00:15:13,280
Nor can I control it.

330
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:14,660
Do you understand?

331
00:15:14,790 --> 00:15:15,320
Yes, I do.

332
00:15:18,450 --> 00:15:20,050
Thank you, Court Pres. Ding.

333
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:23,970
Yingjie.

334
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,360
When you get there,

335
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:27,490
could you bring some books back for me?

336
00:15:28,050 --> 00:15:29,250
If they're too heavy,

337
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:30,220
just mail them.

338
00:15:30,290 --> 00:15:30,960
I'll pay for the postage.

339
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:31,870
I'm not in a hurry anyway.

340
00:15:31,870 --> 00:15:32,200
Okay.

341
00:15:36,510 --> 00:15:37,630
Aren't these books

342
00:15:37,630 --> 00:15:38,890
a bit too basic for you?

343
00:15:39,670 --> 00:15:41,200
They're for Zheng Jianmin.

344
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:42,390
Then why doesn't he ask

345
00:15:42,390 --> 00:15:43,520
Yu Gaoyuan for help?

346
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:44,670
He didn't ask me to do this.

347
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:46,870
I'm the one who wants to buy them for him.

348
00:15:48,670 --> 00:15:50,670
I'm warning you to be careful.

349
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,130
From what I've seen,

350
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:55,300
I don't think Jianmin is that simple.

351
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,120
He's a nice guy.

352
00:15:57,270 --> 00:15:58,600
I'm not saying he's bad.

353
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,080
it's just that...

354
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:01,840
I know.

355
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:03,550
I know you're doing this for my own good.

356
00:16:03,550 --> 00:16:04,670
I just think that

357
00:16:04,690 --> 00:16:06,050
he has helped us a lot,

358
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,340
so this is to thank him.

359
00:16:07,630 --> 00:16:08,080
Fine.

360
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:10,150
You always keep quiet,
but you have strong opinions.

361
00:16:10,150 --> 00:16:10,680
Alright?

362
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:13,390
I'm taking it with me.

363
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:14,520
Stay safe on the way.

364
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:15,200
Okay.

365
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,870
Don't worry. Yu Gaoyuan is going with me.

366
00:16:16,870 --> 00:16:17,670
It'll be fine.

367
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,260
But I'm still worried.

368
00:16:26,030 --> 00:16:28,910
♪ My dear wife ♪

369
00:16:30,870 --> 00:16:31,400
Let's go.

370
00:16:32,750 --> 00:16:33,610
It's time to go.

371
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:37,840
I haven't finished singing for you.

372
00:16:41,310 --> 00:16:41,790
I'll miss you.

373
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:42,670
-I'll miss you.
-Let's go.

374
00:16:42,670 --> 00:16:43,400
I'm leaving.

375
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:44,750
Have a safe trip.

376
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:45,080
Okay.

377
00:16:46,390 --> 00:16:47,080
Be careful.

378
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:47,930
Don't worry.

379
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:50,440
They're not trying to
bring in reinforcements.

380
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:53,240
They're going to
get their marriage certificate.

381
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:54,900
You're talking too much.

382
00:16:59,190 --> 00:16:59,910
Rough.

383
00:17:00,790 --> 00:17:01,720
It means violent

384
00:17:02,670 --> 00:17:03,440
and rude.

385
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:10,720
Firstly,
we need to take a long-distance bus

386
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,349
to the district center.

387
00:17:11,349 --> 00:17:13,349
Then we'll take a train
to the provincial capital.

388
00:17:13,349 --> 00:17:14,880
After that,
we'll take another train to Beijing.

389
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:15,880
It'll be a bit tiring.

390
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,680
It's not tiring. I'm very happy.

391
00:17:19,270 --> 00:17:20,790
Yu! Xia!

392
00:17:22,730 --> 00:17:24,390
Mr. Qin, w-what are you doing?

393
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:25,160
Are you going out?

394
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:27,020
I'm going to Beijing with you two.

395
00:17:27,270 --> 00:17:28,730
I've bought these three tickets for us.

396
00:17:28,730 --> 00:17:29,790
Hurry up. It's time to get on the bus.

397
00:17:29,790 --> 00:17:30,190
You...

398
00:17:31,070 --> 00:17:31,480
Um...

399
00:17:32,150 --> 00:17:33,270
How did he find out about this?

400
00:17:33,270 --> 00:17:34,110
Ask Lu Zeming.

401
00:17:35,970 --> 00:17:37,040
He's so weird.

402
00:17:37,070 --> 00:17:38,400
It's really a bit scary.

403
00:17:38,550 --> 00:17:39,590
It's fine. Let's ditch him
in the provincial capital.

404
00:17:39,590 --> 00:17:40,120
Let's go.

405
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:42,020
Wait a moment.

406
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:46,930
So this is Nanyu?

407
00:17:48,170 --> 00:17:48,960
It's just a tiny place,

408
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:50,090
but it's famous now.

409
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:52,310
What's the name of that lawyer

410
00:17:52,310 --> 00:17:53,440
who is wrongly accused?

411
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:54,110
Li Xiang.

412
00:17:54,930 --> 00:17:55,330
Right.

413
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:56,850
Let's go, Mr. Wang, Mr. Li.

414
00:17:56,850 --> 00:17:58,050
Come on. Let's go now.

415
00:18:20,830 --> 00:18:21,310
Yu.

416
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:22,690
Here you are.

417
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:23,480
No, thanks. I don't need it.

418
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:24,000
No need. Really.

419
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,350
T-Take it. Take it.

420
00:18:25,370 --> 00:18:26,080
Alright.

421
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:27,130
Enjoy your meal.

422
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:31,420
Are you hungry?

423
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:33,220
Let's eat.

424
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:37,510
[Law Department of People's University
of Political Science and Law]

425
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:39,750
[Institute of Law]

426
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:48,280
Let's go, Qin.

427
00:19:48,550 --> 00:19:50,750
Didn't you always dream of coming here?

428
00:19:59,400 --> 00:19:59,880
Qin.

429
00:20:18,070 --> 00:20:18,870
Hurry up, Qin!

430
00:20:35,330 --> 00:20:39,490
[The Spirit of Laws]

431
00:20:57,110 --> 00:20:58,240
The facts are clear.

432
00:20:58,240 --> 00:21:00,300
And the logic is well organized, too.

433
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:02,790
Who wrote these materials?

434
00:21:02,790 --> 00:21:03,920
Yingjie wrote them.

435
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:06,280
We all wrote them together.

436
00:21:13,430 --> 00:21:14,430
You guys are good.

437
00:21:15,550 --> 00:21:16,830
You dare to engage in practice,

438
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:18,070
express your opinions,

439
00:21:18,070 --> 00:21:21,000
stick to your principles
and be loyal to your ideals.

440
00:21:21,030 --> 00:21:23,110
Mr. Cheng and I are both very pleased.

441
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:24,960
I'm still not mature enough.

442
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:27,620
I didn't
think through some things well enough.

443
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:29,590
Who can think everything thoroughly

444
00:21:29,590 --> 00:21:30,720
when they are young?

445
00:21:31,110 --> 00:21:31,640
Gaoyuan,

446
00:21:32,270 --> 00:21:33,550
at critical moments,

447
00:21:33,550 --> 00:21:34,680
you dared to step up.

448
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:35,920
Good.

449
00:21:36,030 --> 00:21:37,430
I just did what I had to do.

450
00:21:38,070 --> 00:21:38,960
As for Yizhong,

451
00:21:39,550 --> 00:21:40,350
he is just

452
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:42,480
a bit too daring.

453
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:45,510
Yizhong always thinks too deeply

454
00:21:46,030 --> 00:21:46,830
about things.

455
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:48,550
Even if he had not

456
00:21:49,030 --> 00:21:49,680
done this,

457
00:21:50,310 --> 00:21:52,590
we would still pay close attention

458
00:21:52,590 --> 00:21:53,720
to Li Xiang's case.

459
00:21:53,830 --> 00:21:55,030
Isn't this our fault?

460
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:56,380
Yizhong must have felt

461
00:21:56,380 --> 00:21:57,440
that he couldn't rely on us

462
00:21:57,440 --> 00:21:58,830
and had no confidence in us.

463
00:21:58,830 --> 00:21:59,490
Look at you.

464
00:21:59,590 --> 00:22:00,030
You're

465
00:22:00,590 --> 00:22:01,830
just partial to him.

466
00:22:03,830 --> 00:22:04,920
But the text

467
00:22:04,920 --> 00:22:06,200
is still a bit lengthy.

468
00:22:07,750 --> 00:22:09,030
I'm worried
that the leaders won't have time

469
00:22:09,030 --> 00:22:10,630
to read such a long document.

470
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:13,480
Come on, Professor Cheng.

471
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:15,270
Why don't you help set the tone?

472
00:22:16,350 --> 00:22:17,590
L-Let me revise it.

473
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:19,590
So this document can be submitted

474
00:22:19,590 --> 00:22:20,650
to the higher-ups?

475
00:22:20,830 --> 00:22:22,920
Will they pay attention to this matter?

476
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:24,580
The country has realized that

477
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:26,580
to achieve long-term stability,

478
00:22:27,750 --> 00:22:30,010
we must follow
the path of the rule of law.

479
00:22:30,230 --> 00:22:33,160
The construction of the legal system
can't be achieved overnight,

480
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:35,360
and it should be developed step by step.

481
00:22:35,750 --> 00:22:38,080
When will the instructions come through?

482
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:40,160
You're even more anxious than I am.

483
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:41,020
Wait a few days.

484
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:43,820
The problem is not as simple as you think.

485
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:45,380
Come on.

486
00:22:45,510 --> 00:22:46,920
Proofread the manuscripts.

487
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:47,250
Okay.

488
00:22:58,730 --> 00:22:59,260
Let's go.

489
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:10,290
Mr. Zhou, Mr. Cheng.

490
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:11,820
This is Mr. Qin Zhigao,

491
00:23:11,830 --> 00:23:13,070
the defense lawyer

492
00:23:13,070 --> 00:23:13,920
of Li Xiang's case.

493
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:14,510
Hello, Mr. Qin.

494
00:23:14,510 --> 00:23:15,310
Hello, hello.

495
00:23:16,750 --> 00:23:17,160
We're leaving.

496
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:17,960
Then we're leaving.

497
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:18,550
Just go.

498
00:23:18,590 --> 00:23:19,170
Bye, sir.

499
00:23:26,510 --> 00:23:26,960
Zhou.

500
00:23:28,590 --> 00:23:29,440
Do you feel that

501
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:30,880
Mr. Qin...

502
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:34,200
What's wrong?

503
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:37,540
Nothing, nothing.

504
00:24:10,480 --> 00:24:11,610
A couple of days ago,

505
00:24:13,480 --> 00:24:15,140
we went to see your three kids.

506
00:24:16,920 --> 00:24:19,650
Your mother-in-law
was taking good care of them.

507
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:23,420
The civil affairs department
of the commune

508
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:25,770
has applied for state subsidies for them.

509
00:24:26,790 --> 00:24:27,680
Your kids will be supported financially

510
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:28,680
until they are 18.

511
00:24:29,270 --> 00:24:29,880
Really?

512
00:24:33,070 --> 00:24:34,670
After their parents' death,

513
00:24:35,310 --> 00:24:36,510
these three children

514
00:24:36,590 --> 00:24:38,520
will be living a good life instead.

515
00:24:40,590 --> 00:24:41,640
Don't worry.

516
00:24:43,070 --> 00:24:44,330
Regarding this money,

517
00:24:45,110 --> 00:24:48,000
your mother-in-law
has to sign her name at the brigade

518
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:48,960
to get it.

519
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:52,180
Others can't take it away.

520
00:24:53,070 --> 00:24:53,960
Thank you.

521
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:55,640
Thanks.

522
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:02,440
Just eat.

523
00:25:17,310 --> 00:25:18,310
It smells so good.

524
00:25:20,110 --> 00:25:21,510
It's really nice in here.

525
00:25:22,550 --> 00:25:24,310
No one hits me or scolds me,

526
00:25:24,750 --> 00:25:26,350
and I don't even have to work.

527
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:28,930
Look. I've even gained weight.

528
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:31,240
Presiding Judge,

529
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:33,110
now,

530
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,480
my hard days are over.

531
00:25:39,030 --> 00:25:40,690
There's also such a good meal,

532
00:25:41,270 --> 00:25:44,200
and you're saying goodbye to me
before my execution.

533
00:25:45,550 --> 00:25:48,750
I haven't lived this life in vain.

534
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:21,460
Why aren't you eating?

535
00:26:23,880 --> 00:26:25,080
I can't bear to eat it.

536
00:26:26,240 --> 00:26:28,270
I want to save it for the kids.

537
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:52,240
Well, regarding this corrupt lawyer case,

538
00:26:52,240 --> 00:26:54,350
why hasn't the procuratorate
initiated a prosecution yet?

539
00:26:54,350 --> 00:26:56,200
They are reviewing the evidence.

540
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:58,400
But the handling prosecutor has said that

541
00:26:58,400 --> 00:26:59,930
there isn't much evidence,

542
00:27:00,070 --> 00:27:01,030
so it's quite difficult to deal with it.

543
00:27:01,030 --> 00:27:02,760
The suspect has been arrested,

544
00:27:02,830 --> 00:27:05,350
but we have to
delay the trial and sentencing?

545
00:27:05,350 --> 00:27:07,640
It has caused rumors to spread everywhere
in our society.

546
00:27:07,640 --> 00:27:09,370
The effect is greatly reduced.

547
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:12,640
Regarding this case,

548
00:27:12,640 --> 00:27:14,880
even if we could
barely manage to convict him,

549
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:17,140
in the future, the verdict will probably

550
00:27:17,330 --> 00:27:18,200
be overturned, too.

551
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:19,590
By that time, maybe

552
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:21,680
each of us will be held accountable.

553
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:23,510
In the end, all of us

554
00:27:24,960 --> 00:27:27,090
will be stuck in an awkward situation.

555
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:28,750
So what do you think we should do?

556
00:27:28,750 --> 00:27:29,960
Since he has been arrested,

557
00:27:29,960 --> 00:27:31,620
why not let the procuratorate

558
00:27:31,790 --> 00:27:33,350
exempt him from prosecution

559
00:27:33,350 --> 00:27:34,280
and release him?

560
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:35,460
We'll release him?

561
00:27:35,790 --> 00:27:38,350
Then what about the authority
of the Party and the law?

562
00:27:38,350 --> 00:27:39,160
Considering this point,

563
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:40,780
I suggested

564
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:42,720
non-prosecution, didn't I?

565
00:27:42,790 --> 00:27:43,270
Well...

566
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:44,680
Guan.

567
00:27:44,750 --> 00:27:46,200
W-What do you think?

568
00:27:46,680 --> 00:27:47,610
Come on. Tell us.

569
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:49,300
L-Let me talk about it.

570
00:27:50,070 --> 00:27:51,440
Actually, non-prosecution

571
00:27:51,440 --> 00:27:52,640
has a deeper meaning.

572
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:53,920
The premise is that

573
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:55,680
the party concerned must be guilty.

574
00:27:55,680 --> 00:27:56,690
But after

575
00:27:56,720 --> 00:27:58,350
being reviewed by the procuratorate,

576
00:27:58,350 --> 00:28:00,830
his crime is deemed noticeably minor,

577
00:28:01,400 --> 00:28:03,070
so he is not prosecuted.

578
00:28:03,840 --> 00:28:05,650
But actually, we've both

579
00:28:05,680 --> 00:28:06,720
found him guilty

580
00:28:07,110 --> 00:28:09,590
and spared ourselves all kinds of trouble

581
00:28:09,750 --> 00:28:10,790
that may be caused

582
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:12,210
by a forced conviction.

583
00:28:13,180 --> 00:28:14,400
Well, I think Court Pres. Ding's idea

584
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:15,600
is really brilliant.

585
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:17,590
It's practical and feasible.

586
00:28:17,590 --> 00:28:19,030
It shows both political wisdom

587
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:20,160
and legal thinking.

588
00:28:20,270 --> 00:28:21,270
In fact, this way,

589
00:28:21,790 --> 00:28:23,450
it's acceptable to everyone.

590
00:28:24,750 --> 00:28:25,550
A few days ago,

591
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:27,640
our region held a meeting

592
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:29,920
on the anti-crime campaign.

593
00:28:31,310 --> 00:28:33,910
Among the 13 counties and cities
in our region,

594
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:35,760
do you guys know

595
00:28:35,790 --> 00:28:36,990
what our ranking was?

596
00:28:38,110 --> 00:28:39,440
You all can take a guess.

597
00:28:39,830 --> 00:28:40,750
What was our ranking?

598
00:28:40,750 --> 00:28:41,880
We ranked 11th.

599
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:44,510
That was second to last.

600
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,130
It was third to last.

601
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:54,450
The main reason

602
00:28:54,480 --> 00:28:55,440
for our poor performance

603
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:56,400
is that

604
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:59,480
we're not resolute in handling
various kinds of chaos

605
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:01,280
and dare not strike hard on them.

606
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:05,750
So there must be a conviction

607
00:29:05,750 --> 00:29:06,640
in this case.

608
00:29:07,070 --> 00:29:08,730
What's more, we have to firmly

609
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:10,440
render a severe and quick judgment.

610
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:11,030
Sir.

611
00:29:11,440 --> 00:29:13,590
If we really turn this case into

612
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:14,970
a wrongful conviction,

613
00:29:15,240 --> 00:29:17,110
and in the future,
they want to hold someone accountable...

614
00:29:17,110 --> 00:29:19,110
I will take all the responsibility.

615
00:29:19,310 --> 00:29:21,200
They can dismiss me if I'm wrong.

616
00:29:21,720 --> 00:29:22,980
What are you afraid of?

617
00:29:26,550 --> 00:29:27,350
Alright then.

618
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:28,920
Well, why are you

619
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:29,650
writing this down?

620
00:29:29,650 --> 00:29:30,070
Um...

621
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:31,070
Does this need to be recorded?

622
00:29:31,070 --> 00:29:32,150
Well, I think this is...

623
00:29:32,150 --> 00:29:34,150
I have it all here. I'm taking notes.

624
00:29:34,570 --> 00:29:34,980
Okay.

625
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:37,200
He has it all, so I'll stop taking notes.

626
00:29:44,110 --> 00:29:45,510
Did you hear what he said?

627
00:29:45,880 --> 00:29:47,140
He has made up his mind.

628
00:29:49,960 --> 00:29:50,560
Oh, right.

629
00:29:54,110 --> 00:29:56,170
Delete the part about dismissing me.

630
00:29:56,340 --> 00:29:57,740
I didn't write that down.

631
00:30:02,550 --> 00:30:03,110
Sir.

632
00:30:04,030 --> 00:30:05,200
I forgot something just now.

633
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:06,720
Put Li Xiang and Hong Zhansheng

634
00:30:06,720 --> 00:30:07,520
aside for now.

635
00:30:07,920 --> 00:30:08,830
As for that college student

636
00:30:08,830 --> 00:30:10,030
who has been arrested,

637
00:30:10,030 --> 00:30:12,090
can we consider letting him go first?

638
00:30:13,270 --> 00:30:13,750
Him?

639
00:30:15,590 --> 00:30:16,750
What's the charge against him?

640
00:30:16,750 --> 00:30:18,600
He can't be charged with anything.

641
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:20,350
After all, he's a top student
from People's University

642
00:30:20,350 --> 00:30:21,550
of Political Science and Law.

643
00:30:21,550 --> 00:30:23,000
He came to Nanyu

644
00:30:23,030 --> 00:30:23,750
for an internship.

645
00:30:23,750 --> 00:30:24,510
Don't let him end up in prison

646
00:30:24,510 --> 00:30:25,830
during his internship.

647
00:30:25,830 --> 00:30:26,290
This...

648
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:28,140
This wouldn't sound good.

649
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:30,880
What do you think?

650
00:30:32,150 --> 00:30:34,080
He's been locked up for seven days.

651
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:36,930
Just consider it as detention.

652
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:38,220
Teach him a lesson.

653
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:40,480
Release him immediately. Okay?

654
00:30:42,110 --> 00:30:43,240
I'll think about it.

655
00:30:44,830 --> 00:30:45,200
Okay.

656
00:31:04,590 --> 00:31:05,200
Cheng.

657
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:08,640
Those kids haven't undergone

658
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:10,590
in-depth legal thinking training.

659
00:31:10,590 --> 00:31:12,160
It's inappropriate to discuss

660
00:31:12,160 --> 00:31:13,440
the death penalty too early.

661
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:14,270
Let's talk about it
when they are postgraduates,

662
00:31:14,270 --> 00:31:14,680
okay?

663
00:31:16,160 --> 00:31:16,480
Well,

664
00:31:16,480 --> 00:31:18,010
you really aren't anxious.

665
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:20,270
Now, because of the Strike-Hard Campaign,

666
00:31:20,270 --> 00:31:21,750
dozens more crimes are suddenly

667
00:31:21,750 --> 00:31:22,950
punishable by death.

668
00:31:24,790 --> 00:31:26,190
Are they all applicable?

669
00:31:27,600 --> 00:31:29,000
If you don't discuss it now,

670
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:30,370
aren't you out of touch with reality?

671
00:31:30,370 --> 00:31:32,400
Being too eager for quick results
is even more out of touch with reality.

672
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:33,640
How am I out of touch with reality?

673
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:34,700
Alright, alright.

674
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:35,550
Come on. Sit for a while.

675
00:31:35,550 --> 00:31:37,210
Your face is covered in sweat.

676
00:31:37,590 --> 00:31:38,000
Let me pour you a glass of water.

677
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:38,880
I can't sit.

678
00:31:38,920 --> 00:31:40,130
You... I'm not thirsty.

679
00:31:40,130 --> 00:31:41,830
No need to get me some water. You...

680
00:31:41,830 --> 00:31:42,240
I...

681
00:31:45,110 --> 00:31:45,790
Mr. Cheng.

682
00:31:46,350 --> 00:31:46,950
Mr. Cheng.

683
00:31:47,830 --> 00:31:48,480
Xia.

684
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:53,460
I'm even scared of you now.

685
00:31:53,790 --> 00:31:55,200
You're here to rush me again, huh?

686
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:56,990
No, we're just here to bring you

687
00:31:57,070 --> 00:31:58,270
the proofread draft.

688
00:31:59,350 --> 00:32:00,070
Yingjie checked it once,

689
00:32:00,070 --> 00:32:00,640
and so did I.

690
00:32:00,640 --> 00:32:01,530
We worked until past 2 AM.

691
00:32:01,530 --> 00:32:02,890
There might be some omissions.

692
00:32:02,890 --> 00:32:03,950
Please take a look.

693
00:32:04,720 --> 00:32:06,180
Thanks for your hard work.

694
00:32:07,310 --> 00:32:08,880
The materials have been delivered

695
00:32:08,880 --> 00:32:10,680
to the central leaders.

696
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:14,350
They need to
learn about the situation thoroughly

697
00:32:14,350 --> 00:32:16,280
and will handle it very carefully.

698
00:32:17,920 --> 00:32:19,050
Give them some time.

699
00:32:19,480 --> 00:32:19,880
Right.

700
00:32:22,030 --> 00:32:22,970
Mr. Cheng

701
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:24,200
also needs some time.

702
00:32:24,480 --> 00:32:25,010
Mr. Zhou.

703
00:32:25,270 --> 00:32:25,920
Mr. Zhou.

704
00:32:26,750 --> 00:32:28,010
Here. Have some water.

705
00:32:29,370 --> 00:32:30,170
Oh, by the way,

706
00:32:30,550 --> 00:32:32,310
I heard that someone
from the National People's Congress

707
00:32:32,310 --> 00:32:33,640
also submitted this case's materials

708
00:32:33,640 --> 00:32:34,550
to the authorities.

709
00:32:34,550 --> 00:32:35,880
They said the materials

710
00:32:36,030 --> 00:32:37,640
were submitted
through the bar association.

711
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:39,700
Lihui must have contributed to this.

712
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:40,320
Right.

713
00:32:41,490 --> 00:32:42,110
Come on. Have a seat.

714
00:32:42,110 --> 00:32:42,550
Don't just stand there.

715
00:32:42,550 --> 00:32:44,200
She's usually so quiet,

716
00:32:44,240 --> 00:32:45,200
but she also participated?

717
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:46,400
We all participated.

718
00:32:48,590 --> 00:32:51,050
We really don't want to
keep rushing you two.

719
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:52,800
It's mainly because
we just got off the phone

720
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:53,790
with our fellows in Nanyu.

721
00:32:53,790 --> 00:32:54,700
They said the county seemed

722
00:32:54,700 --> 00:32:55,960
to be speeding up the process.

723
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:56,980
We're afraid it might be too late.

724
00:32:56,980 --> 00:32:58,240
What are you afraid of?

725
00:32:58,790 --> 00:32:59,310
Even if he's convicted,

726
00:32:59,310 --> 00:33:00,840
it can still be overturned.

727
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:02,400
The leaders have also noticed

728
00:33:02,400 --> 00:33:04,480
the flaws in the law enforcement process.

729
00:33:04,480 --> 00:33:05,790
The development of history

730
00:33:05,790 --> 00:33:07,250
has always been like this.

731
00:33:10,320 --> 00:33:11,240
This also reflects

732
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:13,700
the immaturity
of the current legal system.

733
00:33:14,110 --> 00:33:15,400
Mr. Zhou is right.

734
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:17,700
Though as you can see, Mr. Zhou are now

735
00:33:17,880 --> 00:33:19,140
drafting criminal law

736
00:33:19,270 --> 00:33:20,730
and compiling textbooks,

737
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:23,200
during the Cultural Revolution, he was

738
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:24,270
a reactionary authority.

739
00:33:24,270 --> 00:33:27,110
He cleaned toilets
and was forced into the jet-like posture.

740
00:33:27,110 --> 00:33:28,560
His good friend even...

741
00:33:32,470 --> 00:33:33,030
Mr. Sun.

742
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:34,810
Hello, Professors.

743
00:33:36,030 --> 00:33:36,690
Yu Gaoyuan,

744
00:33:37,270 --> 00:33:38,730
come out here for a moment.

745
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:47,680
Let me ask you.

746
00:33:48,070 --> 00:33:49,070
There's a guy named Qin Zhigao.

747
00:33:49,070 --> 00:33:50,030
You know him, right?

748
00:33:50,030 --> 00:33:51,240
Yes, I do. What's wrong?

749
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:52,310
He was acting like a hooligan

750
00:33:52,310 --> 00:33:54,040
and got caught by the students.

751
00:33:56,750 --> 00:33:57,460
That's him.

752
00:33:58,280 --> 00:33:59,480
He was wandering around the entrance

753
00:33:59,480 --> 00:34:00,110
of the girls' dorm

754
00:34:00,110 --> 00:34:01,370
and acting furtively.

755
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:01,790
No!

756
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:04,020
I just stood there

757
00:34:04,040 --> 00:34:05,170
for a little longer,

758
00:34:05,310 --> 00:34:06,960
and then a few boys surrounded me.

759
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:08,810
I wanted to leave
but they didn't let me go.

760
00:34:08,810 --> 00:34:10,400
If you hadn't peeked through the window,

761
00:34:10,400 --> 00:34:11,330
they wouldn't have surrounded you.

762
00:34:11,330 --> 00:34:12,659
That was the gatehouse.

763
00:34:12,670 --> 00:34:14,320
But you shouldn't have hit him
indiscriminately.

764
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:15,440
We didn't hit him.

765
00:34:15,760 --> 00:34:16,870
He was like this when he was brought here.

766
00:34:16,870 --> 00:34:17,690
It's fine.

767
00:34:18,230 --> 00:34:19,560
They didn't hit me hard.

768
00:34:20,070 --> 00:34:20,510
Sun,

769
00:34:21,150 --> 00:34:22,320
I can vouch for his character.

770
00:34:22,320 --> 00:34:24,150
I'll sign. How about we just let it go?

771
00:34:24,150 --> 00:34:25,370
No need. Thank you.

772
00:34:26,110 --> 00:34:26,480
Okay.

773
00:34:27,280 --> 00:34:28,080
Sign your name

774
00:34:28,280 --> 00:34:29,280
and take him away.

775
00:34:34,440 --> 00:34:35,840
You guys need to pay more attention.

776
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:37,230
Don't let this kind of unemployed person

777
00:34:37,230 --> 00:34:37,920
wander around here anymore.

778
00:34:37,920 --> 00:34:39,570
He's not an unemployed man.

779
00:34:39,710 --> 00:34:40,670
He's a lawyer.

780
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:43,810
With his conduct like that,
he can be a lawyer?

781
00:34:44,630 --> 00:34:45,690
Alright. Let's go.

782
00:34:45,710 --> 00:34:46,510
Qin, let's go.

783
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:47,360
Thank you.

784
00:34:47,480 --> 00:34:48,010
Let's go.

785
00:34:54,920 --> 00:34:56,360
You can't stay at the school anymore.

786
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:57,890
The dorm manager has told me

787
00:34:57,920 --> 00:34:58,760
unauthorized personnel

788
00:34:58,760 --> 00:35:00,480
aren't allowed to enter the student dorms.

789
00:35:00,480 --> 00:35:02,230
I'm really not a hooligan!

790
00:35:02,510 --> 00:35:04,360
Nor am I an unauthorized person!

791
00:35:04,440 --> 00:35:05,630
Why are you guys treating me like this?

792
00:35:05,630 --> 00:35:07,500
Why don't you believe in what I said?

793
00:35:07,500 --> 00:35:09,430
Am I a rag?

794
00:35:09,630 --> 00:35:10,930
Qin! Qin! Calm down!

795
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:11,680
You...

796
00:35:14,440 --> 00:35:16,590
I don't want to say this.

797
00:35:20,230 --> 00:35:21,790
I had thought...

798
00:35:22,240 --> 00:35:24,480
I had thought
if I could come back to take a look,

799
00:35:24,480 --> 00:35:26,840
I would have no regrets in this lifetime.

800
00:35:28,430 --> 00:35:31,030
I really don't want to say this.

801
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:34,230
Just say it.

802
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:36,400
I...

803
00:35:37,220 --> 00:35:40,390
I also graduated from this school.

804
00:35:44,010 --> 00:35:46,420
I'm not a hooligan!

805
00:36:02,510 --> 00:36:03,170
Comrade Su!

806
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:05,920
Comrade Su!

807
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:08,210
What's going on?

808
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:09,480
Comrade Su!

809
00:36:09,870 --> 00:36:10,410
Comrade Su!

810
00:36:10,410 --> 00:36:11,070
You guys can't

811
00:36:11,070 --> 00:36:12,800
lock my son up in there just like this!

812
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:14,030
He's a good boy.

813
00:36:14,150 --> 00:36:15,030
What are you doing?

814
00:36:15,030 --> 00:36:16,000
You guys will be held

815
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:17,550
historically responsible for doing this!

816
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:18,480
As for this problem of mine,

817
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:19,400
I can't explain it to you.

818
00:36:19,400 --> 00:36:19,930
Alright?

819
00:36:20,030 --> 00:36:20,960
Let's go! Let's leave now!

820
00:36:20,960 --> 00:36:21,880
Comrade Su!

821
00:36:21,920 --> 00:36:23,580
Hey, what are you trying to do?

822
00:36:24,070 --> 00:36:24,600
Yizhong.

823
00:36:25,230 --> 00:36:26,560
Help me analyze my case.

824
00:36:27,400 --> 00:36:28,450
I accidentally

825
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:31,120
cut the village's high-voltage cable.

826
00:36:31,320 --> 00:36:32,920
They said it counts as theft.

827
00:36:33,590 --> 00:36:34,450
Accidentally?

828
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,260
How careless could you be?

829
00:36:38,030 --> 00:36:39,090
Then what happened

830
00:36:39,190 --> 00:36:40,250
to the cable later?

831
00:36:40,360 --> 00:36:41,220
Did you sell it?

832
00:36:41,630 --> 00:36:42,230
Yes, I did.

833
00:36:42,480 --> 00:36:43,680
Since you've sold it,

834
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:46,230
the nature of this case
is definitely different.

835
00:36:46,230 --> 00:36:48,290
Obviously, you've committed theft.

836
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:49,450
Yizhong.

837
00:36:49,590 --> 00:36:51,190
Let me tell you about my case.

838
00:36:51,670 --> 00:36:53,440
My girlfriend ran off with someone else.

839
00:36:53,440 --> 00:36:54,920
I went to settle the score with that man.

840
00:36:54,920 --> 00:36:56,480
Unexpectedly, he took out a knife.

841
00:36:56,480 --> 00:36:57,920
I snatched it and stabbed him.

842
00:36:57,920 --> 00:36:59,920
Wasn't that self-defense?

843
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:02,400
Did you go empty-handed?

844
00:37:03,070 --> 00:37:03,510
I...

845
00:37:04,670 --> 00:37:06,080
actually took a stick with me.

846
00:37:06,080 --> 00:37:07,190
But I just wanted to scare him.

847
00:37:07,190 --> 00:37:08,400
What's more, I didn't strike first.

848
00:37:08,400 --> 00:37:09,840
Your intention at that time...

849
00:37:09,840 --> 00:37:10,640
Chen Yizhong.

850
00:37:10,880 --> 00:37:11,230
Here!

851
00:37:14,070 --> 00:37:14,600
Come out.

852
00:37:19,590 --> 00:37:20,110
Buddy,

853
00:37:22,700 --> 00:37:25,100
congratulations to you on being released.

854
00:37:34,550 --> 00:37:36,110
What are you thinking about?

855
00:37:36,110 --> 00:37:38,170
Haven't you stayed here long enough?

856
00:37:38,480 --> 00:37:38,940
Sign it.

857
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:40,770
Just sign it now.

858
00:37:42,280 --> 00:37:43,210
Your mom is here.

859
00:37:43,960 --> 00:37:45,290
She's waiting outside.

860
00:37:45,510 --> 00:37:46,550
In the future, no matter what you do,

861
00:37:46,550 --> 00:37:47,680
don't be impulsive.

862
00:37:49,190 --> 00:37:50,920
Everything has consequences.

863
00:37:51,320 --> 00:37:52,400
If you act recklessly,

864
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:53,730
what about your family?

865
00:37:55,440 --> 00:37:55,920
Sign it.

866
00:37:56,770 --> 00:37:59,300
[Nanyu County Public Security Bureau,
Release Notification]

867
00:38:03,070 --> 00:38:05,200
I'm not a counter-revolutionary man.

868
00:38:25,630 --> 00:38:26,230
Mom.

869
00:38:32,230 --> 00:38:32,890
Look at you.

870
00:38:33,280 --> 00:38:34,190
When you were doing this,

871
00:38:34,190 --> 00:38:35,970
did you think about your father?

872
00:38:35,970 --> 00:38:36,630
Do you know how much injustice

873
00:38:36,630 --> 00:38:38,090
your father has suffered,

874
00:38:38,320 --> 00:38:40,320
and how many sacrifices he has made?

875
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:41,500
Look at you.

876
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:41,960
Just for

877
00:38:41,960 --> 00:38:42,960
such a small case,

878
00:38:43,370 --> 00:38:44,320
you almost ruined

879
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:45,250
your whole life.

880
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:47,230
If you always act so impulsively,

881
00:38:47,230 --> 00:38:49,230
h-how can you achieve great things?

882
00:38:49,550 --> 00:38:50,410
Your father...

883
00:38:52,110 --> 00:38:53,710
M-My father isn't here, huh?

884
00:38:54,320 --> 00:38:55,150
Your father is here?

885
00:38:55,150 --> 00:38:56,480
Who do you think you are?

886
00:38:57,960 --> 00:38:58,230
Mom,

887
00:38:58,260 --> 00:38:59,710
how did you know I was here?

888
00:38:59,710 --> 00:39:00,710
You... Well...

889
00:39:01,800 --> 00:39:02,860
Let's leave first.

890
00:39:03,190 --> 00:39:04,280
Look at your face.

891
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:06,150
Gosh.

892
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:07,710
Which scumbag hit you?

893
00:39:07,710 --> 00:39:09,240
How could he hit you so hard?

894
00:39:09,430 --> 00:39:10,630
I don't know, either.

895
00:39:10,630 --> 00:39:11,960
But who told you about this?

896
00:39:11,960 --> 00:39:14,020
Let's go. We'll talk about it at home.

897
00:39:15,230 --> 00:39:17,560
I remember he seemed to graduate in 1950s.

898
00:39:17,630 --> 00:39:19,230
The Class of 1953.

899
00:39:19,510 --> 00:39:20,600
Here, here, here!

900
00:39:21,230 --> 00:39:21,830
It's here!

901
00:39:23,110 --> 00:39:23,710
It's true.

902
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:24,980
That's him.

903
00:39:25,590 --> 00:39:26,550
His name is right here.

904
00:39:26,550 --> 00:39:27,400
He didn't lie.

905
00:39:29,280 --> 00:39:29,940
Right here.

906
00:39:30,110 --> 00:39:31,510
Look! Right? That's him.

907
00:39:31,920 --> 00:39:32,550
His...

908
00:39:33,510 --> 00:39:35,370
His appearance has changed a lot.

909
00:39:35,710 --> 00:39:36,960
We weren't in the same class,

910
00:39:36,960 --> 00:39:38,320
so we weren't close.

911
00:39:39,030 --> 00:39:40,070
I remember him.

912
00:39:40,760 --> 00:39:42,070
Back then,
I had just stayed on as a faculty member

913
00:39:42,070 --> 00:39:43,030
and was assigned
to the Teaching and Research Office.

914
00:39:43,030 --> 00:39:43,550
Look.

915
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:49,660
How about this?

916
00:39:50,190 --> 00:39:51,320
You two can go ask him

917
00:39:51,510 --> 00:39:53,370
who Corzine and Chugunov are.

918
00:39:54,400 --> 00:39:54,860
Just go.

919
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:07,230
Corzine?

920
00:40:08,710 --> 00:40:10,480
He was the director
of the Teaching and Research Office.

921
00:40:10,480 --> 00:40:12,400
He graduated from the Soviet Union's

922
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:15,110
Sverdlovsk Law Institute.

923
00:40:16,320 --> 00:40:18,450
He was the graduate students' mentor,

924
00:40:19,230 --> 00:40:20,630
so he had never taught us.

925
00:40:22,760 --> 00:40:23,710
Chugunov

926
00:40:25,630 --> 00:40:28,760
was also a Soviet legal expert
who came here to aid China.

927
00:40:29,510 --> 00:40:31,110
On the afternoon

928
00:40:32,670 --> 00:40:34,510
of June 24th, 1955,

929
00:40:37,840 --> 00:40:38,500
right here,

930
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:40,090
right in the cafeteria,

931
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:41,050
at that time,

932
00:40:41,670 --> 00:40:42,270
this place

933
00:40:42,630 --> 00:40:44,290
also served as an auditorium.

934
00:40:45,110 --> 00:40:47,150
He gave us a lecture.

935
00:40:49,320 --> 00:40:50,150
The theme was

936
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:57,710
Principles of the People's Democratic
Legal System in Criminal Proceedings.

937
00:40:59,090 --> 00:41:01,420
The interpreter on the site was Zhou Yipu.

938
00:41:02,150 --> 00:41:03,580
I remember that day,

939
00:41:04,510 --> 00:41:05,370
it was very hot.

940
00:41:12,400 --> 00:41:13,440
Didn't you see it?

941
00:41:14,150 --> 00:41:15,880
Which department are you from?

942
00:41:17,400 --> 00:41:18,480
The Law Department!

943
00:41:18,480 --> 00:41:20,320
Go to the department
and complain about me!

944
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:21,520
My name is Qin Zhigao!

945
00:41:29,760 --> 00:41:30,360
Qin.

946
00:41:31,150 --> 00:41:32,150
Mr. Cheng and Mr. Zhou

947
00:41:32,150 --> 00:41:33,810
want you to go over to see them.

948
00:41:34,360 --> 00:41:35,360
Court Pres. Ding.

949
00:41:35,880 --> 00:41:37,210
Our leader has said that

950
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:39,440
we should eliminate distractions
and focus on the main points.

951
00:41:39,440 --> 00:41:40,960
That college student
has also been released.

952
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:42,070
Now we should focus our efforts

953
00:41:42,070 --> 00:41:43,530
solely on Li Xiang's case.

954
00:41:46,920 --> 00:41:50,070
If you knew it would end up like this,
why did you do it at first?

955
00:41:50,070 --> 00:41:51,550
His mother traveled all the way here

956
00:41:51,550 --> 00:41:52,610
to look for her son,

957
00:41:52,840 --> 00:41:55,150
bringing some reporters
from the provincial newspaper,

958
00:41:55,150 --> 00:41:56,360
who were holding microphones.

959
00:41:56,360 --> 00:41:57,490
And with the cameras

960
00:41:58,320 --> 00:41:58,960
flashing,

961
00:41:59,070 --> 00:42:00,480
who wouldn't be intimidated?

962
00:42:00,480 --> 00:42:01,410
I heard about it.

963
00:42:02,630 --> 00:42:03,590
I heard judging from

964
00:42:03,590 --> 00:42:04,740
the way she dressed,

965
00:42:05,010 --> 00:42:05,800
she looked like

966
00:42:05,800 --> 00:42:06,930
an educated person.

967
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:08,110
But when she was making a scene,

968
00:42:08,110 --> 00:42:09,190
it was truly quite terrifying.

969
00:42:09,190 --> 00:42:09,710
Mr. Sun.

970
00:42:10,360 --> 00:42:11,400
If Chen Yizhong

971
00:42:12,070 --> 00:42:13,840
is really guilty of a certain crime,

972
00:42:13,840 --> 00:42:15,110
no matter who makes a scene,
it wouldn't be useful.

973
00:42:15,110 --> 00:42:16,360
Why should we focus on the main points?

974
00:42:16,360 --> 00:42:17,920
That shows a guilty conscience.

975
00:42:17,920 --> 00:42:20,120
You guys are afraid of messing things up

976
00:42:20,150 --> 00:42:21,550
and causing a bad impact.

977
00:42:22,360 --> 00:42:24,150
We've asked someone
to contact the newspaper office.

978
00:42:24,150 --> 00:42:26,590
The article absolutely cannot
be published.

979
00:42:26,590 --> 00:42:28,280
Our leader's instructions are very clear.

980
00:42:28,280 --> 00:42:29,280
The court and the procuratorate

981
00:42:29,280 --> 00:42:30,360
still need to collaborate well.

982
00:42:30,360 --> 00:42:32,560
Seize the time to prosecute
and convict the suspects.

983
00:42:32,560 --> 00:42:33,730
Don't keep passing the buck like this.

984
00:42:33,730 --> 00:42:34,880
A long delay means trouble.

985
00:42:34,880 --> 00:42:35,740
I'll do my best.

986
00:42:37,810 --> 00:42:38,380
Okay.

987
00:42:44,670 --> 00:42:45,670
How did his mother

988
00:42:45,750 --> 00:42:46,750
figure out that

989
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:48,690
she should go to see our leader?

990
00:42:50,150 --> 00:42:50,630
Yeah.

991
00:42:51,760 --> 00:42:52,420
How about we

992
00:42:53,030 --> 00:42:53,760
look into it?

993
00:42:55,630 --> 00:42:56,160
No rush.

994
00:42:59,440 --> 00:43:00,480
What a smart aleck you are.
